{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/997515-magic-shield-to-revert-damage-on-the-attacker","id":997515,"title":"Magic Shield to revert damage on the attacker!?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-02T19:47:54-07:00","id":997515,"title":"Magic Shield to revert damage on the attacker!?","content":"So, one of my players who is a mage in a dark age's chronicle wants to deal with a vampire with high potence using a kind of magic shield that reverts the damage on the attacker, so the stronger the attack (the vampire in question has Potence 5) the stronger the damage the attacker would suffer with his sword etc...The mage in question is a hermetic one, I know that in Mage the Ascension one would use correspondence to make such a spell, but in the dark ages mage, what Pillars (and levels) do you think would be necessary to use such a spell? The player wants do use his nemesis' confidence in his sheer brute force against himself, which I find cool, given that it must cause a very psychological trauma (and perhaps a lesson), to say the least, in the offender. What do you think of this? Do you think that such a spell could be conceived within any paradigm of dark ages' mage?<br /> Any opinion is welcomed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T22:41:30-07:00","id":997563,"title":"","content":"Any one???","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T14:43:34-07:00","id":997892,"title":"","content":"I'd say Vires 4 to transmute kinetic force applied in one direction into kinetic force applied in the inverse vector, and Anima 3 to lock it on the mage's physical pattern.<br /> <br /> Note that this will look pretty weird - it'd be as if the vampire had punched his own fist. You could use the same Pillars to transmute kinetic force into flame and make the mage's skin fireproof, which might be more mechanically advantageous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7356,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","user":"haldir2012","date":". 11-03-2016, 05:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T15:27:35-07:00","id":997911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haldir2012</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/997515-magic-shield-to-revert-damage-on-the-attacker?p=997892#post997892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say Vires 4 to transmute kinetic force applied in one direction into kinetic force applied in the inverse vector, and Anima 3 to lock it on the mage's physical pattern.<br /> <br /> Note that this will look pretty weird - it'd be as if the vampire had punched his own fist. You could use the same Pillars to transmute kinetic force into flame and make the mage's skin fireproof, which might be more mechanically advantageous.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I see, that would probably look weird, although the vampire in question will probably attack with a sword or claws etc (and perhaps that would look a little &quot;less weird&quot;...)...my player wants to emulate spells that are common on video-games(aka diablo etc lol...), that allows you to reflect damage on the attacker, but it seems such things are hard to emulate using mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T18:41:59-07:00","id":998006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haldir2012</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/997515-magic-shield-to-revert-damage-on-the-attacker?p=997892#post997892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say Vires 4 to transmute kinetic force applied in one direction into kinetic force applied in the inverse vector, and Anima 3 to lock it on the mage's physical pattern.<br /> <br /> Note that this will look pretty weird - it'd be as if the vampire had punched his own fist. You could use the same Pillars to transmute kinetic force into flame and make the mage's skin fireproof, which might be more mechanically advantageous.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the magus, himself, you'd only need to use Vires:3 to redirect most any attack (even of supernatural force/potency) than would typically be encountered (Discipline ratings of 6+, however, might only be partially negated/repelled, unless Vires:4 were used, and that would certainly be the case with Potence:8+ of Methuselah level power). If the Hermetic worked the rote as a daily maintenance spell (not unlike the Parma Magica or similar, in re: Primus:3), then only Vires:3/4 would be required (either as a simple spell, or at a base of 3 successes for duration/resistant ablation, with the excess providing the real protection). If the spell was truly of an indefinite nature, then Anima:2 would be required for (P)attern integration, not Anima:3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T20:08:09-07:00","id":998035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Just John, Forever...</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/997515-magic-shield-to-revert-damage-on-the-attacker?p=998006#post998006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the magus, himself, you'd only need to use Vires:3 to redirect most any attack (even of supernatural force/potency) than would typically be encountered (Discipline ratings of 6+, however, might only be partially negated/repelled, unless Vires:4 were used, and that would certainly be the case with Potence:8+ of Methuselah level power). If the Hermetic worked the rote as a daily maintenance spell (not unlike the Parma Magica or similar, in re: Primus:3), then only Vires:3/4 would be required (either as a simple spell, or at a base of 3 successes for duration/resistant ablation, with the excess providing the real protection). If the spell was truly of an indefinite nature, then Anima:2 would be required for (P)attern integration, not Anima:3.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you very much John! I still think he would be better off using an electric field (similar to the new V20 Way of Levinbolt lv 5) that would melt the blade attacking him before it reached him or cause severe damage to the enemy's claw etc, as in any case, &quot;vulgarity&quot; isn't such a big issue in dark ages mage lol (specially when dealing with &quot;night creatures&quot;). I'm saying this because the rote you suggested still wouldn't be able to completelly protect him from harm (a strong vampire with st 5, potence 5 + a long sword etc can cause a huge amount of damage that would be very hard to completelly negate with the shield, after you use 3 successes only for the duration the rest of the successes wouldn't do much to stop such a huge attack methinks).<br /> <br /> In any case, thank you very much once again! You're a real great contributor to this forum as I've seen you answering these kind of questins many times.<br /> <br /> Cheers,<br /> Daniel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T03:04:46-07:00","id":998157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/997515-magic-shield-to-revert-damage-on-the-attacker#post997515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The player wants do use his nemesis' confidence in his sheer brute force against himself, which I find cool, given that it must cause a very psychological trauma (and perhaps a lesson), to say the least, in the offender.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, a vampire freely advertises their power and their identity to a mage, and seeks to openly squash said mage with direct brute force without relying on thralls, shovelheads or any other kind of proxies. All that, probably, without the backing of any local sphere of power, running the risk of attracting attention and trouble for everyone.<br /> <br /> Plus, since they have Potence 5, I'm safe to assume the vamp is older than the average neonate...This guy isn't confident, he's a moron!<br /> <br /> Damn it, why go to such lengths to teach them a lesson? just light them on fire or run a stake through their heart and hang them for the sun. The other vamps would be grateful to you for that, grateful for ridding them of such a poor excuse of a vampire, of such a disgrace, of such a waste of blood...<br /> <br /> And frankly, teaching them a lesson?...the last thing you want is for that brute to get smarter. Psychological trauma goes a long way toward making that vampire into a proper monster. In the long run, you're not just teaching them a lesson, you're making them a better vampire which, in turn, will make them a more dangerous, more cunning (or less stupid) enemy.<br /> <br /> In other words: kill it with fire! turn them to ash! to ASH!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T03:33:32-07:00","id":998160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/997515-magic-shield-to-revert-damage-on-the-attacker?p=998157#post998157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, a vampire freely advertises their power and their identity to a mage, and seeks to openly squash said mage with direct brute force without relying on thralls, shovelheads or any other kind of proxies. All that, probably, without the backing of any local sphere of power, running the risk of attracting attention and trouble for everyone.<br /> <br /> Plus, since they have Potence 5, I'm safe to assume the vamp is older than the average neonate...This guy isn't confident, he's a moron!<br /> <br /> Damn it, why go to such lengths to teach them a lesson? just light them on fire or run a stake through their heart and hang them for the sun. The other vamps would be grateful to you for that, grateful for ridding them of such a poor excuse of a vampire, of such a disgrace, of such a waste of blood...<br /> <br /> And frankly, teaching them a lesson?...the last thing you want is for that brute to get smarter. Psychological trauma goes a long way toward making that vampire into a proper monster. In the long run, you're not just teaching them a lesson, you're making them a better vampire which, in turn, will make them a more dangerous, more cunning (or less stupid) enemy.<br /> <br /> In other words: kill it with fire! turn them to ash! to ASH!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hahaha I pretty much liked your reply (I love roleplaying <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ), I also think it's easier this way. In any case, the thing is that the game is dark ages and both are pcs and know each other, but they don't know exactly where each other is at the moment. But I know for sure that the vampire is going to try to kill the mage as they had a confrontation earlier in the game and the &quot;strong&quot; vampire likes to crush everything in his way and the mage &quot;offended his pride etc&quot;. What worries my mage player is that if he loses the initiative roll he's probably dead and that's why he came up with ideas of using kinectic shields and forms to protect himself from harm etc (it's not easy to survive a sword attack from a vampire with potence 5 etc...).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T03:57:08-08:00","id":1010139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/997515-magic-shield-to-revert-damage-on-the-attacker?p=998160#post998160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Hahaha I pretty much liked your reply (I love roleplaying <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ), I also think it's easier this way. In any case, the thing is that the game is dark ages and both are pcs and know each other, but they don't know exactly where each other is at the moment. But I know for sure that the vampire is going to try to kill the mage as they had a confrontation earlier in the game and the &quot;strong&quot; vampire likes to crush everything in his way and the mage &quot;offended his pride etc&quot;. What worries my mage player is that if he loses the initiative roll he's probably dead and that's why he came up with ideas of using kinectic shields and forms to protect himself from harm etc (it's not easy to survive a sword attack from a vampire with potence 5 etc...).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> really, I would just kill the sucker. But really, if the PC doesn't know when he'll be attacked he should create a Vires 3 Talisma that would protect him from physical attackes. Maybe even transform it into a flash of light to startle night creatures. or maybe vires 3/corona 1, so the amulet also senses hostile intent nearby, or primus 1 to see corruption of undead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}